profile: minimodel.short-term-memory.v11
updated_utc: 2026-07-02T21:15:00Z
current_state:
  - MiniModel.org is a Rust-first metadata, verifier, and future peer-to-peer tiny model package exchange workspace.
  - Source options are user-owned local files/lists, user-triggered Hugging Face metadata discovery/conversion handoff, one-command `prepare-peer-share` sender packaging, drift-checked catalog-entry writing from manifest plus peer-offer proof, late `add-peer-source` peer availability metadata, portable `write-peer-source-announcement` availability metadata, maintainer-side `apply-peer-source-announcements` drift checks, metadata-only `write-catalog-snapshot` reuse, optional catalog-listed consenting peer sources, direct known-peer HTTP piece serve/fetch, one-command TinyRustLM peer-import request execution, and future broader P2P discovery/relay.
  - First local verifier implementation exists in `crates/minimodel-core` and `crates/minimodel`: manifest parse, boundary rejection, local artifact byte/SHA256 checks, TinyRustLM `.slm` validation, chunk/Merkle verification, `prepare-peer-share` generation of manifest plus `.minimodel-peer-offer` plus local peer pieces plus catalog entry, `write-catalog-entry` proof validation, `add-peer-source` proof-ready entry validation plus one consenting direct peer URL row, `write-peer-source-announcement` availability metadata binding, `apply-peer-source-announcements` model/artifact/proof drift rejection plus peer URL deduplication, `write-catalog-snapshot` metadata-only catalog validation/output, optional `peer_source_count`/`peer_sources` metadata after known-peer URL validation, peer-piece export, direct HTTP peer-piece serving/fetch, peer-piece reassembly, `import-peer-request` receiver execution from TinyRustLM request JSON, and import receipt writing.
  - Local peer pieces are the first transfer bridge: `prepare-peer-share` writes `minimodel.peer_piece_set.v0` plus local chunk files as part of the sender package, `export-peer-pieces` remains available for manual workflows, `serve-peer-pieces` validates and serves only declared sidecar/piece files from a user-started direct HTTP listener, `fetch-peer-pieces` retrieves a piece set and chunks from a consenting direct `http://` peer while rejecting project-server hosts and checksum drift, `assemble-peer-pieces` reassembles only after piece SHA256 checks plus full artifact verification, and `import-peer-request` wraps the receiver sequence for TinyRustLM handoff JSON.
  - Catalog entries now distinguish proof-ready metadata with no known source from proof-ready metadata with a validated `known-direct-http-peer-v0` source: `peer_source_count=0` keeps the TinyRustLM manual known-peer URL gate, while `peer_source_count>0` plus `peer_sources` lets TinyRustLM save a Rust reverify import request immediately without serving bytes from project servers; `add-peer-source` can attach a direct row later without rerunning conversion, while peer-source announcements let a catalog maintainer merge one or more converter availability claims after drift checks.
  - July 2 intake requires beginner UX to stay honest: Hugging Face search returns model cards and metadata, `Start Conversion` creates a local request/script, `P2P Import` appears only for admitted `.slm` metadata with a peer-offer proof and a known consenting peer source, and every import still ends in local Rust checksum plus `.slm` validation and a receipt.
  - Real non-hosted q8 fixture metadata lives at `examples/tiny-test-model-q8.minimodel.manifest.v0`, `examples/tiny-test-model-q8.minimodel-peer-offer`, and generated `examples/catalog-entry.v0.json`; the `.slm` artifact remains outside MiniModel.org.
  - It references MiRust.com as a one-way talisman source.
  - File Handoff setup is initialized with placeholder-only active intake.
  - Public boundary remains no hosted model weights and no server-side inference.
